# TaskFlow project rules

Before coding, read the repository-root AGENTS.md, README.md, docs/README.md, docs/implementation/README.md, docs/implementation/PROJECT-CONTEXT.md, and the relevant existing implementation/theory documents.

AGENTS.md is the canonical source for the full project contract. Follow it.

- TaskFlow theory study and implementation run in parallel. Never require the learner to finish a theory phase before coding.
- The agreed stack direction is React + TypeScript, Node.js + Express + TypeScript, and PostgreSQL. AWS is the later primary cloud direction. Do not silently replace these choices or select undecided libraries without explaining and recording the decision.
- Inspect the real repository state. At the initial setup, the repository is documentation-only; do not claim that source code, runtime, tests, containers, or infrastructure already exist.
- Work in small vertical slices. Do not add speculative frameworks, services, dependencies, or paid cloud resources.
- Documentation is mandatory for every meaningful feature, business rule, architecture/data/API/security change, dependency, infrastructure tool, or new concept. Create or update a beginner-friendly guide under docs/implementation/ in the same change as the code.
- Explain why, what, how, business logic, code locations, concepts, important configuration and commands, failure diagnosis, verification actually performed, trade-offs, and links to related theory lessons.
- Use docs/implementation/templates/implementation-guide-template.md. Keep the implementation indexes and PROJECT-CONTEXT.md current.
- Never claim an unrun test or unverified behaviour. Protect secrets and do not provision or change paid infrastructure without explicit approval.
- Verify relevant tests, changed documentation links, and repository status before reporting completion.
